  "id": "restorative-environment",
  "term": "restorative environment",
  "definition": "A restorative environment is a setting, often natural or nature-like, that helps psychological well-being by lowering stress, renewing attention, improving mood, and supporting everyday recovery. In environmental psychology, it is understood as an environment that actively influences emotional, cognitive, and bodily states through how it is perceived and appraised.",
